# Vue Components

## Component Template

All components use `<script setup lang="ts">` with the Composition API:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'
import { AcButton } from '@alayacare/alaya-design-system'

interface Props {
  title: string
  count?: number
}

const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {
  count: 0,
})

const emit = defineEmits<{
  submit: [value: string]
}>()
</script>

<template>
  <div>
    <h2>{{ props.title }}</h2>
    <AcButton label="Submit" @click="emit('submit', 'done')" />
  </div>
</template>

<style scoped>
</style>
```

## Views vs Components

| Aspect | Views (`src/views/`) | Components (`src/components/`) |
|--------|---------------------|-------------------------------|
| Purpose | Full pages tied to routes | Reusable UI pieces |
| Naming | `*View.vue` (e.g., `DashboardView.vue`) | Descriptive (e.g., `UserCard.vue`) |
| Used by | Router only | Any Vue file |

## Icons

Use **Phosphor Icons** from the Alaya Design System. Always apply two CSS classes: the base `ph` class and the icon-specific `ph-<icon-name>` class.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<i class="ph ph-house" />
<i class="ph ph-arrow-right" />
<i class="ph ph-magnifying-glass" />

<!-- ❌ BAD — don't use inline SVGs or emoji as icons -->
<svg>...</svg>
<span>🏠</span>
```

Size and transform utilities can be added alongside:

```vue
<i class="ph ph-gear ph-lg" />
<i class="ph ph-arrow-left ph-rotate-90" />
```

## Conventions

- Always define props with TypeScript interfaces using `defineProps<Props>()`
- Always type emits using `defineEmits<{ ... }>()`
- Use `<style scoped>` to avoid style leaks
- Prefer Alaya Design System components over raw HTML (see alaya-design-system rule)
- Use `@/` path alias for imports: `import Foo from '@/components/Foo.vue'`
- Use Phosphor Icons (`ph ph-<icon-name>`) for all iconography — custom SVGs are fine for illustrations, but never for UI icons
